Two missing pieces the Qt font and window paths need, and both were silent absences.

CTFontCopyTraits was a stub returning nil. Qt asks the theme font for its traits while building its
font database and reads NSCTFontWeightTrait straight out of the answer, so nil became
CFDictionaryContainsKey(NULL, NSCTFontWeightTrait) and CMake.app died there with CR2 0. macOS always
answers a dictionary for a valid font. The traits builder that CTFontCopyFontDescriptor already had
is now shared between the two, so a descriptor and a direct copy cannot disagree.

This is the same shape as #212, where wxWidgets read the same key out of a descriptor and mmex died
in CFDictionaryGetValue. That one was fixed by making the DESCRIPTOR complete; the direct copy next
to it stayed a stub. Note that 36 of the 57 remaining STUB bodies in CoreText return nil, NULL or 0,
so this class of defect is not exhausted.

NSWindow tabbing did not exist. Qt sets setTabbingMode: on every window it creates, and the
unrecognized selector killed CMake.app inside CMakeSetupDialog before its main window existed.
Nothing in this port tabs windows, so the value is remembered and reported and changes no behaviour;
what matters is that ASKING does not raise. tabbingIdentifier comes with it because the two are one
API and a caller that sets one may read the other.

MEASURED, each fix moving the failure further:
  CFDictionaryContainsKey NULL dict   ->  setTabbingMode: unrecognized selector
  setTabbingMode:                     ->  past window creation, 1560 font descriptors enumerated,
                                          then objc_msgSend +0x29 sending placeAboveWindow: to a
                                          libqcocoa window class whose cache pointer is unmapped

Task #227.

